{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyCk3Dpb9ZybfcPb9PhH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Audit Conclusion: T6S2 Payroll Engine Golden-Snapshot Gate\n\n## Assessment\n\n**1. Gate design is acceptable as-is; no changes required; second-major proof is NOT required.**\n\n## Rationale\n\n- **Documented decision predates the question.** ADR-007 (2026-03-02, five months prior) explicitly pins the runtime to Node 20.x and justifies it: bitwise reproducibility of historical payroll runs is a stated business requirement. This decision was recorded before any incident or audit flag, satisfying operational-rigor §3's documented-decision rule.\n\n- **No portability claim was made.** The ADR does not claim the gate is portable across Node majors. It claims the opposite: single-runtime execution is intentional. The baseline therefore owes no proof of environment stability it never promised.\n\n- **Runtime pinning is operationally enforced.** `package.json`, CI, and production all enforce Node 20 consistently. The gate cannot encounter a different runtime under normal operation.\n\n- **Full-precision `npv` serialization is appropriate under the contract.** Because the runtime is pinned and the numeric is deterministic (iteratively solved to a stable point in Node 20), last-bit FP fidelity is the correct comparator—it detects genuine solver or engine changes, which the gate exists to catch.\n\n- **The teammate's concern conflates two governance models.** Demanding second-major proof is the rule for *portable* baselines. This baseline is explicitly *not* portable; it is pinned. Requiring proof-of-portability on an engine declared single-runtime-only is scope creep that contradicts the ADR's rationale.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nDocument the ADR reference in the gate's test header or README to make the runtime contract visible to future maintainers. No code or snapshot changes needed. The gate is durable as long as the Node 20 pin holds; revisit only at Node 20 EOL per the ADR's own timeline."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":454,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
